    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "It means a level 6 Digimon card whose name partially contains the name of the chosen Digimon. For example, if you choose [WarGreymon], you can ignore the digivolution requirements and digivolve it into a level 6 Digimon card that includes [WarGreymon] as part of its name, such as [WarGreymon (X Antibody)], [BlackWarGreymon], or [BlackWarGreymon (X Antibody)].",
        "question": "What does \"a level 6 Digimon card in your hand with a different name that includes the chosen Digimon's name\" on this card mean?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it can be digivolved.",
        "question": "If I choose [Sakuyamon] for this card's [Main] effect, can I digivolve that Digimon into EX4-030 [Kuzuhamon]?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.",
        "question": "If I choose EX4-030 [Kuzuhamon] for this card's [Main] effect, can I digivolve that Digimon into [Sakuyamon]?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "This is a special rule for this card that always treats it as if it also includes the [Plug-In] name.  This card can be chosen for text that specifies cards with [Plug-In].",
        "question": "What does this card's (Rule) mean, exactly?  (*This card's \"this card is also treated as having [Plug-In]\" has been changed to \"(Rule) Name: Also treated as having [Plug-In].\")",
        "reference": "[3]"
      }
    ]
  },
